                    </div>
                    <p> My involvement in robotic football in freshmen year focused mainly on practical 
                        application and skill development. I honed my soldering skills working on LED strips and 
                        took on the reconstructing the Pi Hat PCB that connects the Raspberry Pi and power the smaller 
                        electronics. This involved bringing the design to Git and creating and correcting 
                        the generated Bill of Materials (BOM) and Component Placement List files from KiCad. 
                        These files were then successfully exported for JLCPCB manufacturing, 
                        ensuring the accurate production of our component 
                    </p>

